<Doc
  title="Sub20 compared with HandBrake, LosslessCut and online compressors"
  description="What Sub20 does that HandBrake, LosslessCut and online video compressors don't, and what each of them does better."
  current="compare"
  heading="Sub20 compared with HandBrake, LosslessCut and online compressors"
  lead="Sub20 does one job: trim a clip and fit it under a size. The tools below do more, or other things. This is where each one fits."
>
  <div class="table-scroll">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><td></td><th scope="col">Sub20</th><th scope="col">HandBrake</th><th scope="col">LosslessCut</th><th scope="col">Online compressors</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><th scope="row">Aims at a file size</th><td>Yes, and checks the result</td><td>No: you set quality or bitrate</td><td>No</td><td>Some do</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Trim before encoding</th><td>Two handles on a filmstrip</td><td>By time or frame numbers</td><td>Yes, its main job</td><td>Some do</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Encodes on the graphics card</th><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td><td>Cuts without encoding</td><td>On their servers</td></tr>
